            <ArticleTitle>Unicompartmental osteoarthritis of the knee: an innovative osteotomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>148-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thirty patients with unicompartmental osteoarthritis of the knee and genu varum deformity ranging from 2 degrees to 15 degrees were treated with high tibial osteotomy by using a medial open wedge, stabilized and distracted with our fixator. Pain relief and correction of deformity were achieved in all except two cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
